note right of DashboardWidget
Represents the configured widget instance
placed on a dashboard layout.
end note

note right of AppUser
Voice assistants use account-linked bearer tokens
resolved at request time.
No Alexa-specific identity is persisted yet.
end note

note right of WidgetSnapshot
Stores the resolved content displayed
for a widget at a specific point in time.
Denormalises widget type and title so
historical snapshots remain readable even
if widget configuration changes later.
end note

note right of SnapshotGenerationJob
Tracks idempotent widget snapshot commands.
Used to coalesce duplicate RabbitMQ deliveries,
record retries, and mark stale jobs skipped.
duplicate_skip_count and last_duplicate_at retain
evidence of coalesced duplicate deliveries.
lease_expires_at permits recovery of abandoned
PROCESSING work after a worker failure.
The logical key is widget_id + snapshot_date
+ requested_config_hash.
dashboard_id, tenant_id, and user_id are retained
scope identifiers without separate foreign keys in
the current Prisma model.
end note

note right of DashboardBriefingGenerationJob
Tracks dashboard-audio commands independently from
widget jobs, including idempotency, retry evidence,
duplicate accounting, and a recoverable processing lease.
RabbitMQ quorum queues provide durable at-least-once
delivery, TTL retry backoff, and terminal dead lettering;
this table remains authoritative for job state.
end note

note bottom of Connector
Tenant-level integration configuration,
for example weather, calendar, email, RSS, or news.
Secrets stay outside Postgres and are
referenced through secret_ref.
end note

note right of AppUser
Stores persisted profile details and
delivery preferences that must survive
auth token refreshes. Telegram is the
first implemented audio-delivery channel.
Profile images are currently stored as
base64 data on the user record.
Preferred language is also stored here so
every LLM prompt can target the user's
chosen output language.
end note

note bottom of BriefingSnapshot
Recommended unique key:
(user_id, dashboard_id, snapshot_date)
end note

note right of DashboardBriefing
Dashboard-level derived artifact built
from the latest eligible widget snapshots.
Stores the structured script contract and
the source hash used for cache reuse.
end note

note right of DashboardBriefingPreference
Controls whether dashboard audio briefing
is enabled and how it should sound.
Widget instance overrides still control
which widgets contribute content.
end note

note right of TenantAiConfiguration
openai_api_key is a deprecated compatibility column.
Runtime code must neither read nor write it. OPENAI_API_KEY
is injected from a root-owned mode-0600 environment file
outside immutable releases; the selected model remains
non-secret tenant configuration in PostgreSQL.
end note

note right of DashboardBriefingAudio
storage_key is relative metadata. Audio bytes belong
in the persistent AUDIO_BRIEFING_STORAGE_DIR mount
shared by backend and worker, not inside a container layer.
end note

note bottom of ApplicationLogEvent
Independent operational event table; it has no foreign key
to tenant or user in the current Prisma schema.
end note

@enduml
